From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:38:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: ML noise reduction on the neural
 engine (draft)

On H16-family ISPs (J616s and J700) macOS runs the camera low-light ML
noise reduction, ISP algorithm 0x143d, on the platform neural engine.
The ANE driver loads the per-board network into the ANE and both
firmwares exchange work over a pair of 16 KiB rings. The ISP driver
allocates the rings, maps them into its IOMMU, passes them to the ANE
driver and tells its firmware with CISP_CMD_IPC_ENDPOINT_SET2.

Add the ISP side and the in-kernel interface to the ANE driver
(include/linux/soc/apple/ane-isp.h):

- find the ANE from the "apple,ane" phandle and name the network after
  the board (apple/ispane-<board>.afpp);
- after the firmware starts, allocate the ring pair, ask the ANE driver
  to load the network and set up its endpoint, then send 0x300c;
- unset the endpoint (0x300d) before the firmware stops;
- per stream, enable 0x143d only when the endpoint is live. Enabling it
  without one stalls the stream, so a missing network, ANE or doorbell
  leaves the camera exactly as before.

The doorbell each side uses to signal the other is not known yet, so no
SoC sets ane_doorbell_known and nothing changes at runtime until it is.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit c5b5d15953f00c83e45f9fa4e9a3b38f51023ebe)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
